course: dictionary
lesson: 7104
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary word can have more than one meaning. Pear can name a fruit, a tree, or a shape. Read the sentence first, because the words around it show which meaning the writer wants. «Each bag has 5 pears» means the fruit you can count, not a tree.
explain: «Pear-shaped» describes a shape: narrow at the top and wide at the bottom, like the fruit. Add «go» and the meaning changes completely. In the UK, «go pear-shaped» means go wrong. Ask yourself whether the sentence makes sense with your meaning. If it does not, try another one.
explain: Friends use jokey slang to laugh at their own mistakes: «it all went pear-shaped». Nobody means a fruit here. The context tells you that things went wrong, which is what the friends are laughing about.
fact: A pear is a sweet, juicy fruit, narrow at the top and wide at the bottom.
fact: Pear skin can be green, yellow or brown.
fact: A pear tree is the tree that grows pears.
fact: «Pear-shaped» means narrow at the top and wide at the bottom.
fact: In the UK, «go pear-shaped» means go wrong.
exercise: «Each bag has 5 pears.» What does pear mean here? | A tree that grows in a field | A shape with a narrow top | A kind of bag | *A sweet, juicy fruit
exercise: Friends say «it all went pear-shaped». What does it mean? | *Things went wrong | The day was sunny | Everything was shaped like a fruit | Everything tasted sweet
exercise: Pears grow from flowers and hold seeds in the core. Find and copy the word that names the middle of the fruit where the seeds sit. | skin | tree | juice | *core
test: «The pear tree in the garden is covered in flowers.» What is a pear tree? | A fruit with a narrow top | *A tree that grows pears | A kind of slang | A bag for carrying fruit
test: Mia says a pear is a kind of bird. Is she right? | Yes, pears fly in flocks | Yes, but only in the UK | *No, a pear is a sweet, juicy fruit | Yes, pears are a type of songbird
exam: «The plan went pear-shaped when the bus was late.» What does pear-shaped mean here? | A tree in the park | A sweet snack | *Went wrong | Shaped like a fruit
